      "seed": 960769801,
      "version": 375,
      "versionNonce": 328804679,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1780812351218,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "For such systems, we generally have 2 storages\n    - Core Database (It can be POSTGRES, or DYNAMODB both can works)\n    - Blob storages (like Amazon S3, which actually stores the raw bytes)\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "For such systems, we generally have 2 storages\n    - Core Database (It can be POSTGRES, or DYNAMODB both can works)\n    - Blob storages (like Amazon S3, which actually stores the raw bytes)\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
