    {
      "id": "JH4VwLePxj76S21Kgbis0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -343.2070305051353,
      "y": 2659.7729045930782,
      "width": 667.339599609375,
      "height": 550,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0e",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 118704873,
      "version": 1071,
      "versionNonce": 1619729929,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1780828964695,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Important part is, how we sync across multiple devices\nThere are 2 scenarios that we have to cover to fix this\n\n1. Local - Remote\n   - for this, there are already builtin methods\n     provided by the OS to detect any changes to \n     the local dropBox folder (fileSystemWatcher in windows\n     and FSEvents in MacOS)\n  - When they detect any changes in the folder\n    it will use upload API to upload all the changes to the remote\n\n2. Remote - Local\n   - This can be detected by couple of ways\n   - one is through webSockets (SSE) which will\n     continously pushes notifications if something changes\n     but this is redundat\n   - Another is Periodic Polling to the server\n     Periodically polling the server (every few minutes)\n     and checks whether something changes using our API\n    it it detected if updateAT timestamp was changed\n  - We will use hybrid approach both WebSocket and Polling\n  - Then we will use out download API to get all the changes locally",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Important part is, how we sync across multiple devices\nThere are 2 scenarios that we have to cover to fix this\n\n1. Local - Remote\n   - for this, there are already builtin methods\n     provided by the OS to detect any changes to \n     the local dropBox folder (fileSystemWatcher in windows\n     and FSEvents in MacOS)\n  - When they detect any changes in the folder\n    it will use upload API to upload all the changes to the remote\n\n2. Remote - Local\n   - This can be detected by couple of ways\n   - one is through webSockets (SSE) which will\n     continously pushes notifications if something changes\n     but this is redundat\n   - Another is Periodic Polling to the server\n     Periodically polling the server (every few minutes)\n     and checks whether something changes using our API\n    it it detected if updateAT timestamp was changed\n  - We will use hybrid approach both WebSocket and Polling\n  - Then we will use out download API to get all the changes locally",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
